          "review_id": "Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tSRk5rNW5aMDkwZHpSS1l6TXpaa2hWTW1WNVpGRRAB",
          "review_text": "I find it hard to understand how this has such high ratings. To me - as a regular fine diner -\nit’s a highly overrated restaurant. For 500 dollar for two for the tasting menu at least one should also get great service (besides great food). Instead the waiters just put plates in front of you, mumble a quick description and leave. There is no effort to establish rapport with the guests or an effort to make the guests feel great. Very disappointing. The food was good but felt too robotic - a series of neat plates, some quite tasteful but delivered with little charm. We were done with the menu within 2 hours. Again at this price level one can expect much more in terms of experience. Furthermore they seem to have a sewage problem as it smelled like that - especially downstairs. And it was uncomfortably cold in the upstairs dining room due to the air-con both which is why I rated low on atmosphere. The place does look nice though and there are lovely details in cutlery and plating.\n\nOverall not worth booking 3 months ahead and spending this kind of money on. Go elsewhere.",
